<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Emirate of Bukhara</h1><p class="st-meta">1785 CE – 1920 CE · capital Bukhara</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Manghit state of Bukhara, a conservative Islamic emirate that survived as a Russian protectorate until the Red Army stormed its capital in 1920.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-rahim-of-bukhara">Muhammad Rahim</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manghit-dynasty">Manghit</a> tribe took real power in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khanate-of-bukhara">Khanate of Bukhara</a> in the 1740s under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah's</a> protection. In 1785 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-murad">Shah Murad</a>, a pious ruler, set aside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janid-dynasty">Janid</a> figurehead khans and took the title emir, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> ruled through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbeks">Uzbek</a> tribal chiefs, a clerical elite and officials, enforcing Islamic law strictly. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a> had hundreds of mosques and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">madrasas</a> and was a centre of trade in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a>, karakul and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a>. Emir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasrullah-khan-emir-of-bukhara">Nasrullah</a> executed the British officers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-stoddart">Stoddart</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arthur-conolly">Conolly</a> in 1842. Wars with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khanate-of-kokand">Khanate of Kokand</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khiva">Khiva</a> were frequent.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">Emir</a> Muzaffar in 1868, taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a> and making <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a> a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>. In 1920 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/young-bukharans">Young Bukharans</a> stormed Bukhara, the last emir, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammed-alim-khan">Alim Khan</a>, fled to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/islamic-emirate-of-afghanistan-2021-present">Afghanistan</a>, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bukharan-peoples-soviet-republic">Bukharan People's Soviet Republic</a> was founded.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/emirate-of-bukhara.jpg" alt="Emirate of Bukhara" width="320" height="211"><figcaption>Image: CentralAsianEditor, Fish bowl · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Emirate_of_Bukhara-Buxoro_Amirligi_Bayrog%27i.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1785 CE – 1920 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bukhara</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Shah Murad, Nasrullah Khan, Alim Khan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Persian, Uzbek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>, <a href="/countries/tajikistan">Tajikistan</a>, <a href="/countries/turkmenistan">Turkmenistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bukharan Emirate, Manghit Emirate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1852&amp;focus=emirate-of-bukhara" aria-label="Emirate of Bukhara on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6268 754 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Emirate of Bukhara lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" 